    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All references are consistent. The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic from `(lastName, postcode)` and rewired every household-keyed rule accordingly. The work is spread across small, single-responsibility units in the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline:\n\n**`HouseholdNormalizer`** (the shared source of truth)\n- `id(lastName, postcode)` now returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (dropped the old `H-` prefix and the address-based key).\n- Added `belongsTo(Owner, householdId)` so all three consuming steps decide household membership through one place instead of copying the comparison.\n\n**`AssignHousehold`** \u2014 shrank to one job: stamp the deterministic `householdId` on *every* owner. No repository scan, no `sharesHousehold` dependency, so owners with the same last name + postcode share it automatically.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity`** (the duplicate block) \u2014 now rejects with 409 when an existing owner shares the computed `householdId`, **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold`, which bypasses the block so the owner is created as a declared household member.\n\n**`CountHousehold`** \u2014 counts members by shared `householdId` (was last name + address).\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared member (`sharesHousehold`) is never flagged; otherwise it flags on shared household + different telephone, keyed off `householdId`.\n\n**Supporting cleanups** \u2014 `DuplicateIdentityException` now carries the offending household id with an accurate message; `IdentityKey` / `OwnerMapper` / `openapi.yml` docs updated so `identityKey` reads as a read-only contact summary and the `householdId` + `sharesHousehold` descriptions match the new behaviour.\n\n`sharesHousehold` no longer creates the link (the link is now automatic and deterministic) \u2014 it only bypasses the duplicate block, exactly as specified.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` acceptance test passes: two owners with the same last name + postcode share a household id (the second via `sharesHousehold`), and a different last name yields a different id.",
